\'93We should be safe in the quarter. It\'92s not too far out of our way.\'94 He said happily, a huge smile exposing his unusually straight and white teeth, all his own. No mean feat considering the diet and hygiene of the lows. \'93I had a mongrel of a time blocking off that drain. How the hell did you manage it?\'94\
\'93You blocked it off? I can\'92t believe you did it.\'94 Her eyes nervously glancing at the doorway, a mere few metres behind them, but there was no sign of flooding.\
\'93You didn\'92t? You were very specific, \'91Make sure you block the drains\'92.\'94 Cracker used the high-pitch whiny tone that all men employ when lampooning a female voice.\
\'93I diverted the water instead.\'94\
\'93Thanks for the heads up\'94\
\'93How did you manage it?\'94\
\'93Chucked in anything I could find. Towels, chairs, mops and buckets and finally some crazy fat guy jumped on top of it all, shouting \'91Power to the people, comrades.\'92 I left when the crowd gathered.\'94\
\'93A communist rally.\'94 She said nodding knowingly. \'93If he gets reported, he\'92s as good as dead.\'94 Impromptu or not, a communist rally was a communist rally.\
\'93Same for us, I fear\'94\
\'93A good time to make haste.\'94
